{number: 117}
{title: Hail to the Brightness}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Hail to the brightness of Zion's glad [Bb7] morning,
[Eb] Joy to the lands that in [Ab] darkness have [Eb] lain!
Hushed be the [Bb7] accents of [Eb] sorrow and [Bb7] mourning,
[Eb] Zion in triumph be-[Ab] gins her mild [Eb] reign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Hail to the brightness of Zion's glad [Bb7] morning,
[Eb] Long by the prophets of [Ab] Israel fore-[Eb] told;
Hail to the [Bb7] millions from [Eb] bondage re-[Bb7] turning!
[Eb] Gentiles and Jews the blest [Ab] vision be-[Eb] hold.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Lo, in the desert rich flowers are [Bb7] springing,
[Eb] Streams ever copious are [Ab] gliding a-[Eb] long;
Loud from the [Bb7] mountain tops [Eb] echoes are [Bb7] ringing,
[Eb] Wastes rise in verdure and [Ab] mingle in [Eb] song.
{end_of_verse}
